#     .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest drafts/research_tests/test_h0221_design_effect.py -q
#     .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest drafts/research_tests/test_research_math.py -q -k design_effect
#
# WHAT IT FIXES
#   compute_design_effect used an ANOVA/ICC estimator whose within-cluster sum of
#   squares (m * p_cluster * (1 - p_cluster)) is exactly 0 when every month is
#   unanimous. The `if wss == 0: return 1.0` guard on the next line then reported
#   NO clustering for the most pseudoreplicated sample possible, so deff PEAKED at
#   90% within-month agreement and COLLAPSED at 100%:
#
#       agreement   OLD deff   NEW deff
#             70%      3.441      3.491
#             90%     13.196     13.964
#            100%      1.000     21.818     <- the collapse
#        all-hit      1.000     20.000     <- degenerate p == 1
#
#   The replacement is a MIRROR of tools/accuracy_registry.py:design_effect (and of
#   daemon/internal/clusterstat.DesignEffect, which SWARM 3 PART A verified is the
#   same estimator) over months instead of days — not a third estimator. Both of the
#   grader's guards come with it: degenerate p returns the worst case n/k, and the
#   result is floored at 1.0.
#
# CHANGES NO PUBLISHED NUMBER.
#   Nothing imports h0221 (grep over the tree: only drafts/research_tests reference it).
#   research/eighty/h0221.py is a standalone script whose compute_design_effect feeds
#   only its own EFFECTIVE_N stdout line. The published intervals come from
#   tools/accuracy_registry.py and daemon/internal/clusterstat, neither of which is
#   touched here and neither of which ever had this defect.
#
# SAFETY: read-only with respect to the live DB, the daemon and git state. The file
#   is NOT in the preserved research/eighty/h026[5-9].py range and is not on the
#   locked-file list.
